From cdb6540b702006e00dcd1d8f38f958bf535d6c5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chang Liu <cliu1004@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [FlyDSL] Vendor BF16 paged decode for Qwen3.8 QSA
 attention

Qwen3.8's post-compaction sparse attention runs through CK's group-mode
prefill kernel on ROCm, which puts a length-one decode query on 1 of 128
MFMA rows. FlyDSL's pa_decode_tile flattens query_length * query_group_size
onto M and splits KV across CTAs; vendored under aiter.ops.flydsl.kernels.pa
with the public entry in aiter.ops.flydsl.pa_decode.

From amd-nprotaso/aiter qwen_3_8_improvement: 7e47471a and ae6497e1.
